[57.987114, "o", "    ✓ note — System python (/usr/local/bin/python3 = 3.13.1) had pip's di\r\nFixed.\r\n\r\n## What was wrong\r\n\r\nNot a permissions or config problem — pip's actual code was missing.\r\n\r\n```\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/\r\n├── pip-24.3.1.dist-info/   ← metadata present\r\n└── (no pip/ directory)     ← the package itself was gone\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo `/usr/local/bin/pip3` existed and ran, but died on its first import:\r\n\r\n```\r\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'\r\n```\r\n\r\nSomething deleted the `pip/` package directory while leaving its `dist-info` behind. This also meant the usual repair, `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, silently no-opped with *\"Requirement already satisfied: pip\"* — it saw the stale metadata and assumed pip was installed.\r\n\r\n## What I did\r\n\r\n1. Moved the orphaned `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` aside (backup kept at `/tmp/pip-24.3.1.dist-info.broken.bak`).\r\n2. Ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which reinstalled pip 24.3.1 from the bundled wheel in `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensu"]
[57.987142, "o", "repip/_bundled/` — no network needed.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- `pip3`, `pip`, `pip3.13` all report `pip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)`\r\n- `pip3 check` → `No broken requirements found.`\r\n- Real install works: installed `six` to a scratch target and imported it successfully (`1.17.0`)\r\n- All 852 files listed in pip's `RECORD` now exist — the installation is complete, not just importable\r\n\r\n## Two things worth knowing\r\n\r\n**`/usr/bin/python3` (3.11) has no pip at all**, and it's marked `EXTERNALLY-MANAGED`, so Debian intends for you not to install into it directly. I left it alone. Use `/usr/local/bin/python3` (3.13) — it's first on your `PATH`, so plain `python3`/`pip3` already resolve there.\r\n\r\n**You're running pip as root into the system interpreter**, which is what let a bare `rm` break it in the first place. For anything you actually need, `python3 -m venv` will keep future damage contained. If you want, I can also raise pip to 26.2.2 — it flagged that upgrade"]
[57.987233, "o", " as available, but I didn't apply it since you didn't ask and the version you have now works.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=17 surface=103984024bca\r\n"]
